[[File:Cannon.png|thumb|Cat Cannon]]

==About==
*The Cat Cannon is part of the [[Cat Base]].
*It looks like a cat with a cannon for a mouth. It sits on top of the [[Cat Base]].
*It is a weapon that gradually recharges over time. Once it's fully charged, it can be activated to unleash a special attack, which varies on the cannon equipped.
*Cannon heads are created, upgraded, and equipped using the [[Ototo Corps]].
*By default, this weapon can be very useful against [[Assassin Bear]] and other basic enemies at level 10 since it can mow them down in one hit.
*A "Fire!!" button in the bottom right hand corner is used to activate the Cat Cannon's attack.
**It has a charge time, which is divided into ten bars. Every few seconds, one bar fills up, the speed of which depends on the Cat Cannon Charge upgrade and Cat Cannon Attack upgrade, as well as the [[Turbo Machine]]/[[Mysterious Force]]. The minimum charge time is 31.67 seconds as of [[Version 6.1 Update|Version 6.1]], but can be shortened further through the use of Cat Cannon Charge [[Talent Orbs|Ability Orbs]].
*The max range of the Cat Cannon is 6,000. The Cannon can reach the end of most stages as most stages have a width of 6,000 or less. There are exceptions such as [[Dictator's Garden]].
*The Cat Cannon does 1,550 damage without any Treasures at level 20+10, and 4,550 with all Treasures under the same condition.
*Overall, the cat cannon is a versatile superweapon (although not to be left to defeating entire bosses), that the enemies lack! Well, most of the time...

==Cannon Types==
*The '''Default Cat Cannon''' shoots a beam, followed by explosions creating a [[Wave Attack]] that does low to medium damage and has a slight knockback effect. While the knockback is not as significant as that of Cat units, it can knock back enemies that are normally immune, although any enemies that can negate waves are not affected.
*The '''Slow Beam''' fires a harmless green beam across its range, slowing all non-immune enemies it hits. Upgrading the Slow Beam will increase the amount of time enemies are slowed for.
*The '''Iron Wall''' deploys a blue wall in front of the frontmost enemy unit, blocking enemies. The Iron Wall itself is a Cat unit with the Metal trait (which makes it take 1 damage from non-critical hits), does not attack, and ''does'' take up a slot in the Cat limit. The wall will vanish after a set duration or upon absorbing excessive damage. Upgrading the Iron Wall increases the HP of the summoned wall and its duration.
*The '''Thunderbolt''' cannon calls down a lightning bolt in front of the frontmost Cat unit deployed, dealing damage to all enemies in a radius as well as freezing all non-immune enemies hit. Upgrading the Thunderbolt increases the freeze duration.
*The '''Waterblast''' cannon fires a blast of water that crashes down in front of the frontmost Cat unit deployed, damaging [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal Enemies]] by a percentage of their current health. '''<u>Non-metals only lose 0.1% of their current health when hit, rounded up, usually resulting in just 1 damage.</u>''' Upgrading the Waterblast increases the percentage damage done to Metals.
*The '''Holy Blast''' fires a golden beam across its range. On hit, [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie Enemies]] within range take percent-based damage scaling with their maximum health and are briefly frozen while also suffering a knockback effect similar to the default Cat Cannon. Burrowed zombies will be forced to resurface while taking significantly higher damage. It also has the Zombie Killer and Soulstrike abilities, allowing it to finish off zombies and hit those that are yet to revive. <u>'''Non-zombie foes are immune to this cannon.'''</u> Upgrading the Holy Blast increases the percentage of max health damage done to Zombies and its freeze duration.
*The '''Breakerblast''' cannon creates an explosive blast in front of the frontmost enemy unit, dealing damage in a radius as well as causing a knockback effect. Unlike the basic cannon, the Breakerblast is able to affect Wave Immune enemies and Zombies that are yet to revive, but not those that are knockback immune. The Breakerblast will also instantly destroy the barriers of all enemies it hits, hence its name. Upgrading the Breakerblast increases the radius of the explosion and the damage dealt.
*The '''Curseblast '''cannon fires a harmless beam of lightning across its range, cursing all non-immune enemies hit by it. Upgrading the cannon increases the amount of time enemies are cursed for.
*For more strategies involving the different cannon types, see [[Ototo Corps]].

==Uses==
*The Cat Cannon is usually used to clear out peons and chip away at boss enemies.
*From level 10 and up, the Cat Cannon will be strong enough to kill [[Assassin Bear]]s, making it the best way of dealing with them.
*The default Cat Cannon and Holy Blast forces targeted enemies to flinch on hit. This can help [[Cheese]] certain levels with timing. They and Breakerblast can be used to interrupt enemies with long attack animations, like [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]].
*The Thunderbolt Cat Cannon can stop enemy units for a very limited amount of time, which can help with fast-attacking bosses that are breaking through your meatshields.
*Since the power upgrade also increases recharge time, some niche strategies rely on not upgrading it (or leaving it at level 9+10) for shorter recharge time. However, this is not beneficial for the majority of players.
**This will prevent you from upgrading the cannons with Ototo past level 10, resulting in lower overall slow uptime with the slow beam, not enough damage from the regular cannon to snipe certain Assassin Bears and so on, but it will allow for more common attack interruptions with the basic and breakerblast cannons, more "forced un-burrows" and more openings for well timed attacks.

